Installation
------------

sideRETRO uses Meson build system to manage configuration and compilation process.
To build and install sideRETRO, type the following commands:

    $ meson setup build
    $ meson compile -C build
    $ meson test -C build          (optional: run the tests)
    $ meson install -C build       (optional: install)

zlib, HTSlib and SQLite3 are used from the system if found. Otherwise,
they are downloaded, compiled and statically linked into sideRETRO.
The unit tests need libcheck, and the other tests need Python 3.

By default, sideRETRO will install under '/usr/local'.
Choose another prefix when configuring the project:

    $ meson setup build --prefix=$HOME/.local

or change it, and see the other options, in an already configured
build directory:

    $ meson configure build
    $ meson configure build --prefix=$HOME/.local

You may need to execute "meson install -C build" as root
(i.e. sudo meson install -C build) if installing to system directories.

For more details about Meson, please visit https://mesonbuild.com/.
